---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="Support" description="Support and contact for the BullDozer app — world statistics, country profiles, maps and a data quiz.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px">
      <span class="kicker">Help</span>
      <h1>BullDozer — Support</h1>
      <p class="sub">Last updated: 28 July 2026</p>

      <p>BullDozer is a free app and website that turns public statistics into
      charts, country profiles, maps and a data quiz. This page is where you
      get help.</p>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Contact</h3>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:agent@azenha.ai">agent@azenha.ai</a>
        — questions, bug reports, or a number that looks wrong. Please mention
        your device and the app version, it makes problems much easier to
        trace. We usually reply within a few days.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Do I need an account?</h3>
        <p>No. The app has no sign-up, no login and no ads.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Does it work offline?</h3>
        <p>Yes. Datasets are cached on your device after the first load, so
        charts and country profiles keep working without a connection. Fresh
        data is fetched whenever you are online.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Where does the data come from?</h3>
        <p>From public statistical sources, republished as open data files at
        <a href={`${base}/`}>azenha.ai/bulldozer</a>. Every dataset page
        names its source and the period it covers.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>A figure looks wrong</h3>
        <p>Tell us which indicator, country and year, and we will check it
        against the source. Public statistics are revised over time, so a
        number may legitimately differ from one you saw elsewhere.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>A country is missing from a chart</h3>
        <p>Coverage varies by indicator — not every source reports every
        country for every year. Gaps in the source stay gaps in the app rather
        than being filled with estimates.</p></div>

      <div class="gloss-term"><h3>Privacy</h3>
        <p>The app collects no personal data. See the
        <a href={`${base}/privacy`}>privacy policy</a>.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
